# Invoke Despair at an opponent who controls no creature, enchantment or planeswalker: all three sacrifices are impossible, so
# each time they lose 2 life and Bot1 draws a card (CR 701.21a, the spell's text). Bot2 loses 6 and Bot1 draws 3. The process is
# repeated whether or not the earlier sacrifice was possible.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Swamp
Black Lotus
Invoke Despair
Island x3
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Plains x27

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Invoke Despair.Cast(Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 14
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
Bot1.Graveyard = Invoke Despair; Black Lotus
